# Security headers for impact-mapping.
#
# THIS APP'S OWN COPY. It is deployed by the appliedvibe.ai website-publisher
# repo, whose apps/impact-mapping shell sets "sharedAssets": false: the app
# brings its own design system (1,248 lines of CSS, its own tokens, light and
# dark) and wants none of Pico, the riso tokens or the fonts. The publisher's
# `npm run sync` therefore never touches this file — re-check it whenever
# website-publisher's shared/_headers changes.
#
# The /* section is IDENTICAL to shared/_headers, deliberately. The app needed no
# relaxation: it makes no network calls, loads nothing from a CDN, uses only
# system fonts, and its PNG export goes through a data: URL, which the shared
# `img-src 'self' data:` already permits. If you add a directive here, say
# which line differs and why, the way block-royale's _headers does.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; manifest-src 'self'; media-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(self), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

# Vite content-hashes every file it emits under /assets/, so each URL is
# immutable by construction: a changed file gets a new name. Never extend this
# to index.html or any unhashed path, or a deploy goes unseen until the cache
# expires. (website-publisher HANDOFF.md §7 #13.)
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
